ng White to respond\n- It controls key central squares (b4, c3, e3, f4, b6, c7, e7, f6)\n- It maintains flexibility for my development\n- From d5, the knight exerts maximum pressure and cannot be easily dislodged by pawns\n- It's an active move that seizes the initiative rather than passively developing\n\n**Answer:** N: f6-d5"}
