ly the queen or other pieces. But **N: d4-c2** specifically forks the king AND the rook on a1, which is immediately winning material.\n\nReason: \nN: d4-c2 delivers check to the White king on e1 while simultaneously attacking the rook on a1. This is a classic knight fork. White must respond to the check by moving the king, after which I can capture the rook on a1 with Nxa1, winning the exchange (rook for knight) which is approximately a 2-point material advantage. This is a decisive tactical blow.\n\nAnswer: N: d4-c2'}
