e:\n1. It attacks f2, which is only defended by the king\n2. White's king is stuck in the center and vulnerable\n3. This creates immediate threats that White must address\n4. It's a developing move that improves piece activity\n5. Forces White into a defensive position rather than allowing their knights to dominate\n\nAnswer: B: e7-h4"}
